<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Fyodorov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510–<a href="/years/1583">1583</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Fyodorov was a printer who, with Pyotr Mstislavets, produced the Apostol of 1564, the first precisely dated book printed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. Forced to leave Moscow soon afterwards, he continued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, at Zabłudów, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> and Ostroh, where he produced the Ostrog Bible of 1581, the first complete Bible printed in Church Slavonic. He is honoured as the founder of printing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p></div>
